A||||11||TylerB11||85 GT - my first fiero!||||1||
Z||000000||TylerB11||07-03-2001||10:45 AM||||I just bought my very first fiero this weekend. A white 85 GT that runs like a dream. There are a few minor problems that I'm having. I've searched the forum, and have found many answers but I'm missing a few.<P>The "Check Engine Light" has been coming on about 10 seconds after starting the car. I've checked the codes with the car "on" but not running (as directed) and all I get is 12. Should I try it with the car running? How about reseting the ECM by taking off the negative battery terminal? THe car runs perfect so I don't know what it is. (actually the Idle seems a little high at 2000 - is that right?)<P>Second - that damn up shift light is annoying as hell - I hear you can disable it in the ECM using a laptop and the ALDL connection..any truth to that?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||07-03-2001||11:04 AM||||Congrats on your new toy!<P>I'm not sure what can turn the light on without setting a code. If there really are no codes it should keep flashing 12 over and over. Re-check just to make sure there are no codes. All resetting will do is remove any codes already there.<P>2000 is a little high when cold but not anything to worry too much about. as long as it goes down around 900-1000 after it warms up.<P>I didn't know the upshift light was used on V6 cars. It doesn't on my 88. It would probably be easier to just remove the bulb though. The back of the instument pod comes off with 5 size 15 torx on the top and 2 7mm screws on the bottom. Figure out which bulb it is and take it out. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TylerB11||07-03-2001||12:34 PM||||Thanks for the help!<P>With the CEL, am I not getting the right reading because I'm checking the light without the engine running?<P>Another Q - has anyone mounted a front license plate on a 85 GT? there is no real place for it - it either covers up the the front intake or scrapes the ground if lower. I'm in NJ so its required..any Ideas?<P>After I posted that I realized, duh, take the Shift indicator bulb out.<P>The Idle is consistantly around 2000 - a smoooooth 2000, but 2000 nonetheless. Would an Idle screw adjustment be the fix?<P>Side note - It takes a bit to get used to driving with non-antilock brakes again, I locked up the brakes at a stoplight for no apparent reason :-)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||07-03-2001||12:40 PM||||There isn't a user servicable idle adjustment screw.  you must have a vacuum leak somewhere.  The EGR tube is the major cause of vacuum leaks on the V-6s. Wiggle it and see if the idle changes.<P>I believe there is a front license plate bracket on E-bay right now.<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593009955&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593009955&r=0&t=0</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||07-03-2001||03:51 PM||||Congrats on your new car!<P>I would carefully check all your vac hoses and the hard plastic hoses for any leaks or breaks.  Those along with the EGR tube are the most common cause of vac leaks.  Your idle should start around 2000 rpm when cold but settle down to about 700 (auto in gear) to about 900 (manual or auto in neutral).  The Fiero is very hard on vac hoses due to the high engine compartment temperature.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||07-03-2001||04:09 PM||||Checking for codes with the engine off is the right way.  If you jumper the aldl connector with the engine running, the light will flash at different rates to indicate whether or not the engine is in "closed loop" mode and also to show whether the O2 sensor is seeing a "rich" or "lean" condition.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steven||07-03-2001||04:26 PM||||I almost hate to ask, because I don't want to insult you in case you already know this. But you do know that it will flash the code three times before moving on to the next code?||||reg||1
Z||000007||85blackgt||07-03-2001||11:16 PM||||cool man my first fiero was a 85gt as shown above! but now ive upgrated to a 86se!!!<P>congrats dude have fun with it i know i did!<P>------------------<BR>it's for the better your better half is gone. It's ok you didn't need her anyway. and i don't wanna  hear you say nobody can take her place and what more kan i say you didn't need her anyways.! -less than jake<P>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6||||reg||1
Z||000008||TylerB11||07-04-2001||01:18 PM||||Hey Guys, thanks for all your help.<P>I cleared the ECM then ran it until the CEL came on. Checked the codes and got a 14. I'm assuming that is the temp sensor right by the thermostat housing, correct? Is there any history of a wiring problem or just a bad sensor?<P>After Changing all the plugs, wires, distributor cap and oil/oil filer, it runs even better, and the idle has dropped to 1500. I've been checking the vacuum lines, but with no luck so far. I still have to check the EGR, and I'm hoping that is the culprit.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Sootah||07-04-2001||02:20 PM||||Have you actually been pulled over for not haveing a front Licence plate? If not, then DONT put it on!! There so blasted ugly! They are required here in Utah and my buddys never been pulled over for it. (He was pulled over right after he bought the car, he didnt have plates yet and the rear window is tinted so even standing right begind the car you couldnt see the temp paper)||||reg||1
Z||000010||286SE'S||07-06-2001||03:44 PM||||Forget Ebay unless you want salvage yard junk. The Fiero store sells a new license plate holder for 25.00||||reg||1
